    <string name="lang_privacy">Privacy</string>
    <string name="lang_privacy_10_body">DevLedger uses application security measures including authentication, device-level security and protected communication with connected services.\n\nNo software system can guarantee absolute security, and users remain responsible for protecting access to their devices and accounts.</string>
    <string name="lang_privacy_11_body">You may manage supported preferences through the Settings screen, including language, notification and security settings.\n\nWhere supported by the application, account and profile information may also be updated or removed.</string>
    <string name="lang_privacy_12_body">This Privacy Policy may be updated as DevLedger develops or as its services change. The latest version will be made available through the application.</string>
    <string name="lang_privacy_13_body">Questions regarding this Privacy Policy can be directed to the DevLedger development team.</string>
    <string name="lang_privacy_1_body">DevLedger may collect information that you provide when creating and using an account, including your name, email address, profile information and application preferences.\n\nThe application may also store information that you create through its features, including code snippets, folders, tags and financial tracking records.</string>
    <string name="lang_privacy_2_body">DevLedger may use email authentication and third-party Single Sign-On providers such as Google and GitHub.\n\nAuthentication providers may supply DevLedger with limited account information required to identify and authenticate you. DevLedger does not require access to your third-party account password.</string>
    <string name="lang_privacy_3_body">DevLedger may use biometric authentication or a PIN to protect access to sensitive application features.\n\nBiometric verification is performed through supported Android device security mechanisms. DevLedger should not directly store raw fingerprint or facial biometric data.</string>
    <string name="lang_privacy_4_body">Information is used to provide application functionality, authenticate users, manage user preferences, store developer assets, display financial records, synchronise data and improve the reliability of the application.</string>
    <string name="lang_privacy_5_body">DevLedger follows an offline-first design. Certain information may be stored locally on your device so that core functionality remains available without a network connection.\n\nLocal information may later be synchronised with DevLedger\'s cloud services when connectivity becomes available.</string>
    <string name="lang_privacy_6_body">Account and application data may be transmitted to DevLedger\'s REST API and stored in its linked database for synchronisation and account access purposes.\n\nAppropriate safeguards should be used to protect data during transmission and storage.</string>
    <string name="lang_privacy_7_body">DevLedger may integrate with services including Google, GitHub and Firebase.\n\nThese providers may process limited information required to provide authentication, notifications or other connected functionality. Their own privacy policies apply to information processed by those services.</string>
    <string name="lang_privacy_8_body">If notifications are enabled, DevLedger may use Firebase Cloud Messaging to deliver application alerts and reminders.\n\nNotification preferences may be changed through the application\'s Settings screen.</string>
    <string name="lang_privacy_9_body">Financial records entered into DevLedger are used to support the application\'s personal income and expense tracking functionality.\n\nUsers should avoid entering unnecessary sensitive banking or payment credentials into free-text fields.</string>
    <string name="lang_privacy_policy">Privacy Policy</string>
