    <string name="lang_terms_10_body">The collection and handling of personal information is explained separately in the DevLedger Privacy Policy.\n\nYou should review the Privacy Policy before creating or using a DevLedger account.</string>
    <string name="lang_terms_11_body">These Terms &amp; Conditions may be updated as DevLedger develops. Where appropriate, the latest version will be made available through the application.</string>
    <string name="lang_terms_12_body">Questions regarding these Terms &amp; Conditions can be directed to the DevLedger development team.</string>
    <string name="lang_terms_1_body">DevLedger is a personal developer utility and asset vault designed to help users manage code snippets, developer assets, financial records and related application preferences.\n\nDevLedger is currently an academic application prototype and may contain features that are still under development.</string>
    <string name="lang_terms_2_body">You are responsible for providing accurate account information and for protecting access to your account.\n\nYou must not knowingly allow another person to use your account credentials. You should immediately take appropriate action if you believe your account or authentication credentials have been compromised.</string>
    <string name="lang_terms_3_body">DevLedger may use email authentication, Single Sign-On services and device-level biometric or PIN verification to protect access to your account and stored information.\n\nYou are responsible for maintaining appropriate security on the device used to access DevLedger.</string>
    <string name="lang_terms_4_body">You remain responsible for information that you create, upload or store through DevLedger, including code snippets, configuration information and financial records.\n\nYou should not store content that you do not have permission to use or content that violates applicable laws or third-party rights.</string>
    <string name="lang_terms_5_body">DevLedger must not be used to intentionally store, distribute or manage malicious, unlawful or unauthorised content.\n\nYou must not attempt to interfere with the application, its authentication services, REST API, database, synchronisation services or other connected systems.</string>
    <string name="lang_terms_6_body">DevLedger may synchronise locally stored information with its cloud services when network connectivity is available.\n\nSynchronisation may occasionally be delayed or unavailable because of connectivity problems, service maintenance or technical errors.</string>
    <string name="lang_terms_7_body">Some DevLedger functionality may rely on third-party services such as Google, GitHub and Firebase.\n\nUse of these services may also be subject to the terms and policies of the respective third-party providers.</string>
    <string name="lang_terms_8_body">DevLedger\'s financial tracking functionality is intended as a personal organisational tool.\n\nInformation displayed by DevLedger should not be considered professional financial, accounting or tax advice. Users remain responsible for verifying their own financial records.</string>
    <string name="lang_terms_9_body">Reasonable efforts are made to keep DevLedger available and functional. However, uninterrupted access cannot be guaranteed.\n\nFeatures may temporarily become unavailable because of maintenance, connectivity problems or technical issues.</string>
